  faqs: [
    { question: "Where does IB Gram find an IB tutor for a family based in Imphal?", answer: "We start from your child's programme, subject and level, then pull a shortlist from tutors across India who have taught that exact course, since Imphal itself has no local IB school to draw on. Fit is judged on syllabus experience first, not location, and the lesson time is fixed around your household only after that. Nothing gets booked before a free trial lesson, and a different tutor comes in if the first pairing does not click." },
    { question: "Can my child in Imphal get a Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE tutor?", answer: "Yes, on either board. A tutor teaches strictly to the Cambridge or Edexcel specification your child has chosen, over video rather than at your address, since neither board currently runs at a school inside the city. Matching goes down to the code and tier, such as Extended Mathematics 0580 or Chemistry 0620, using that board's own past papers and mark schemes throughout." },
    { question: "Will a tutor actually come to our house in Imphal?", answer: "No tutor visits an Imphal home. House calls exist only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR; a family here gets a live, one-to-one video lesson with a shared whiteboard instead, which is a genuine form of tuition from home rather than anyone travelling to it. Every subject, IB or IGCSE, is delivered this same way." },
    { question: "How much does IB or IGCSE tuition run for a family in Imphal?", answer: "Rates move with the programme, subject and level chosen, how long a session runs, and how recently a tutor has taught that specific syllabus, with the final figure confirmed before your trial lesson. Diploma subjects at Higher Level generally cost more than Cambridge Core-tier support does. Since every lesson is online, travel adds nothing to the bill, and stopping or pausing sessions never carries a penalty." },
    { question: "Does any school inside Imphal actually teach IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Not at present. Schools such as Don Bosco School, Johnstone Higher Secondary Public School and the city's Kendriya Vidyalayas follow CBSE, ICSE or Manipur's own BOSEM and COHSEM boards. A family after an IB or Cambridge/Edexcel qualification either sends a child to board outside the state or works with a tutor while the child stays enrolled in Imphal." },
    { question: "My son boards outside Manipur at an IB school. Can tutoring fit around his term breaks?", answer: "It regularly does, and it is one of the most common reasons Imphal families reach out, given that no school in the state teaches the Diploma or Middle Years Programme. A tutor is matched to whatever subject, level and syllabus the boarding school actually follows, then scheduled around holiday dates or, if the school allows it, an evening slot during term." },
    { question: "Do we get to see a lesson before agreeing to anything?", answer: "Every family gets a free trial lesson first. The tutor works through a genuine topic from your child's own syllabus over video, at no cost and with no obligation to book further sessions. Afterward comes a short plan for the opening month, which you can accept, ask to be adjusted, or set aside for a different tutor entirely." },
    { question: "Will a tutor write parts of my child's IB Internal Assessment for them?", answer: "No, that crosses a line IB Gram will not cross. A tutor's role covers helping pick a workable research question, unpacking what each assessment criterion is actually looking for, planning how data gets collected, and reading drafts honestly, but never producing the written work itself, since that would break IB's own academic integrity rules." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects does IB Gram cover for students connected to Imphal?", answer: "Coverage spans the subject groups a boarding student from Imphal is most likely to be carrying: both Maths routes at HL and SL, the three sciences, Economics, Business Management, English A, Computer Science, plus the compulsory Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay core." },
    { question: "Is tutoring available for the Middle Years and Primary Years Programmes too, not just the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, right across the continuum, for Imphal households whose child is enrolled at an IB school elsewhere or picking up a curriculum for the first time. MYP sessions concentrate on criterion-level analysis in the sciences and languages plus the Personal Project journal; PYP sessions build reading, number sense and the research skills the Exhibition eventually calls for." },
    { question: "Given there is no IB school nearby, does an online tutor really compare to in-person help?", answer: "For Imphal it compares favourably, mainly because a genuinely qualified in-person alternative for these subjects does not exist locally to compare against. A shared digital whiteboard, marked-up past papers and recorded worked examples replicate almost everything a tutor sitting beside your child would otherwise offer, while widening the search for the right specialist to the whole country." },
    { question: "How does IB Gram check a tutor before introducing them to us?", answer: "Every tutor is screened on formal qualifications, how recently they have taught the exact subject and level in question, and how they approach marking against published criteria, before a family ever meets them. Because Imphal has no resident IB or IGCSE teaching pool to lean on, recency of experience with that precise syllabus weighs especially heavily. The trial lesson then lets you form your own judgement." },
    { question: "What is a sensible time to start IB or IGCSE tutoring from Imphal?", answer: "Beginning at the start of the course, Class 11 for the Diploma or Grade 9 for Cambridge/Edexcel IGCSE, gives foundations time to settle before internal assessments, predicted grades and IA deadlines start arriving together. A family starting later, even in the final year, can still gain real ground once sessions focus tightly on the highest-value topics and timed past papers." },
    { question: "We want to move our child from CBSE onto IGCSE. Is that something a tutor can manage?", answer: "It is a request IB Gram sees fairly often, since no Imphal school runs both boards side by side for a family to compare directly. What usually needs the most work is not content but exam technique: command words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' carry specific expectations that CBSE rarely trains for, so a term of preparation ahead of the actual switch pays off." },
    { question: "Are evening or weekend slots realistic for an Imphal household?", answer: "Most families here settle into weekday evenings after school, plus weekend mornings, and that pattern works fine online. Scheduling flexes around the monsoon months when a family might prefer an earlier slot, and around occasions such as Yaoshang or Ningol Chakkouba when the household calendar shifts for a few days. Adding an extra session before mocks takes no more than a message." },
    { question: "What if the tutor and my child simply are not a good match?", answer: "Tell us, and we arrange someone else. Every family gets a check-in every few weeks specifically to catch this early, rather than leaving a child to struggle through with the wrong tutor. Since nothing here runs on a fixed contract, changing tutors or pausing sessions altogether never costs anything extra." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram have any partnership with a school in Imphal, or with the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "None at all. IB Gram operates independently of every school mentioned on this page, and of the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education and Pearson Edexcel alike. Those names appear here only to describe how Imphal's education system actually works, and tutors simply follow whichever board or programme a family's child is already on." },
  ],

